# Task1 source work and memory ledger — UNEXECUTED

Scope: isolated Float64/Int stable packed U, host Int64, n64..4096; b<=8, h=b+1, w=n-r+1. No production routing, adapter, factorization, solves, driver, Julia parsing/compilation or allocation/time measurements. Counters are explicit source operations, not allocator instrumentation. Existing source objects use ordinary imports; no method overwrite. Runtime/compiler/allocation acceptance remains open.

## Preconditions and next-task boundary

Task2 alone performs original validated spike preparation, begin/invalidation, incidence initialization/replacement and column rotation before the first panel; handles one-rejection-per-update latch, original scalar suffix, sticky `decision.finite == false`, busy/exclusive update, prepared two-RHS ownership, update/history append and finish. Before r, elimination is complete: columns j<r have no stored band entries in r:r+b. Packed indices are unique, sorted logical rows with common owned row order; positions/column_order are inverse permutations, incidence rows ready and sorted. Structural tests use these actual production types, not an alternative packed implementation. The minimal carrier deliberately has no backend/solve, so it cannot qualify API/lifecycle behavior.

Helpers accept only Float64 stable packed columns for admission. Gather intentionally allows sparse micro-panels for structural tests; caller must perform `_bgb_eligibility` before workspace construction in the real route. No whole-matrix validation scan is added to a hot helper. Reentering an unfinished workspace and committing into another upper-vector owner are rejected. Concurrent or external mutation of the same owner between gather and commit is prohibited by the adapter contract. No hidden O(nnz) hash/validation. A failed gather must discard workspace in Task2. Commit releases owner in finally; catches only to invalidate/rethrow, never to retry.

