## Source operations by execution frequency

| Phase / frequency | Explicit work | Allocation / retention |
|---|---|---|
| Dimension rejection / attempted first panel | O(1), no packed scan | no workspace construction; zero allocation is a prospective test |
| Eligibility / attempted panel | two binary interval searches per w columns, comparisons counted; read each stored band value until invalid or completion | fixed decision/counters; no vectors |
| Gather / admitted panel | repeat two searches per column; initialize h*w values +2*h*w mask positions; read/write stored band values and presence | reuse workspace; cold constructor separately |
| Apply / <=b steps | current pivot check, strict comparison, one division; swaps2*w value stores +4*w mask stores; at most sum(w-t) FMA and finite tests, each with one value store and2 mask stores; one explicit below-diagonal value store and2 mask stores per step | eight fixed history slots; no growing ledger |
| Commit cost prepass | two searches/w column, h*w support mask inspections plus compared original row indices; calculate exact planned stores, no mutation/column allocation | scalar totals only |
| Budget rejection | no writeback, reserve or fresh column allocation | clear private owner/phase; Task2 performs original scalar suffix once |
| Incidence reserve / admitted commit | h*w mask probes to compute h final lengths; h sizehint! requests | ordinary row growth/coexistence additional |
| Column commit | repeat support searches and h*w comparisons; unchanged nn value stores; changed2*new_length index/value stores (prefix/suffix source reads separately); <=w interval merges | changed columns2 arrays each, sequential publication |
| Incidence rebuild | clear h rows; ONE ascending n stable-ID pass, mapping positions; h*w masks and exactly final-band-nnz pushes | existing row vector capacities, <=h grows |
| History / cache publication | NOT Task1: Task2 skips identity steps, appends once, calls original finish on whole success | existing history/pools additional |

Combined commit stores are checked against2*h*w BEFORE any reserve/column allocation. No resize!/insert!/delete! occurs on changed packed column branch. Support-read/gather/search work is outside this store cap and is not omitted. Counter17 counts prefix/suffix copied source elements; new band values/physical IDs are read from tile/order and charged by the store count, not counter17. With valid packed columns, all whole-column copied payload is bounded by accepted stores; allocator traffic is not.

One ascending stable-ID loop costs O(n+h*w), not O(h*w) alone. Across p=O(n/b) panels, repeated searches cost O(n² log n/b), arithmetic/masks/accepted stores O(n²), ID passes O(n²/b), plus original incidence growth/history/backend work. A rejected panel adds its preflight/gather and at most8 attempted steps before scalar replay. A sparse rejection can still regress time; no speedup inferred. First rejection disabling blocking is a Task2 obligation, not enforced by stateless eligibility itself.

## Counter schema (1-based tuple fields)

1 preflight stored-value reads; 2 binary-search calls; 3 binary comparisons; 4 gathered stored entries (each value read/store plus row-index read); 5 value zero initialization stores; 6 logical mask writes; 7 swapped value stores; 8 FMA calls (each also finite check/value store); 9 attempted pivot steps (one division only after finite/nonzero checks); 10 support mask inspections; 11 planned commit stores; 12 completed commit stores; 13 completed pair-of-array allocation requests; 14 peak logical old/new column payload; 15 stable-ID visits; 16 incidence pushes; 17 copied prefix/suffix source elements; 18 committed column intervals; 19 cleared incidence rows; 20 reserve mask probes.

Array request counter records after both allocations succeed, so it is NOT allocation-attempt/failure accounting; Task2 failure instrumentation must record preforward requests separately. Scalar field writes, branches, tuple-counter rebuilding and bounds checks are additional fixed/control costs. NoCounts removes diagnostic counter updates by dispatch; this is source intent, not an inference/zero-allocation proof. Counted probes and uncounted timing must be separately bound in future admission. Bit writes are logical operations, not native memory instructions. Commit phase/owner writes and exception metadata are cold/constant costs. No artificial counter is a full backend-work budget.

